    "height": 25.62,
    "size": 21
  },
  {
    "slide": 20,
    "text": "BACKUP / SIZE AND COMPLEXITY",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 24,
    "width": 860,
    "height": 13.42,
    "size": 11
  },
  {
    "slide": 20,
    "text": "Repository size describes scope, not understanding",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 52,
    "width": 872,
    "height": 35.2,
    "size": 32
  },
  {
    "slide": 20,
    "text": "git 901f2c64 \u00b7 Monthly first-parent snapshots \u00b7 Tracked .py files \u00b7 Includes tests, drivers and vendored files",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 501,
    "width": 803,
    "height": 12.2,
    "size": 10
  },
  {
    "slide": 20,
    "text": "20",
    "x": 875,
    "y": 500,
    "width": 36,
    "height": 14.64,
    "size": 12
  },
  {
    "slide": 20,
    "text": "File-edit entropy describes concentration of edits. It is not a code-complexity score.",
    "x": 55,
    "y": 457,
    "width": 850,
    "height": 21.96,
    "size": 18
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "BACKUP / COMPARISON LIMITS",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 24,
    "width": 860,
    "height": 13.42,
    "size": 11
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "What this case study can establish",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 52,
    "width": 872,
    "height": 35.2,
    "size": 32
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "Explicit evidence limits \u00b7 The absence of a counterfactual does not prevent reporting concrete outcomes",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 501,
    "width": 803,
    "height": 12.2,
    "size": 10
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "21",
    "x": 875,
    "y": 500,
    "width": 36,
    "height": 14.64,
    "size": 12
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "Available evidence",
    "x": 68,
    "y": 159,
    "width": 383,
    "height": 24.4,
    "size": 20
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "Completed research components\nHistorical failure / repair pairs\nRepository activity and scope\nThe speaker's own recollections",
    "x": 68,
    "y": 197.4,
    "width": 383,
    "height": 97.6,
    "size": 20
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "Not measured",
    "x": 509,
    "y": 159,
    "width": 383,
    "height": 24.4,
    "size": 20
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "A matched no-AI baseline\nHuman hours saved\nA controlled model ranking\nA learning score",
    "x": 509,
    "y": 197.4,
    "width": 383,
    "height": 97.6,
    "size": 20
  },
  {
    "slide": 21,
    "text": "Release dates and commit counts alone cannot identify model-specific productivity gains.",
    "x": 55,
    "y": 436,
    "width": 850,
    "height": 56.12,
    "size": 23
  },
  {
    "slide": 22,
    "text": "BACKUP / UNCERTAINTY COMPONENTS",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 24,
    "width": 860,
    "height": 13.42,
    "size": 11
  },
  {
    "slide": 22,
    "text": "Compare the sources released with the paper",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 52,
    "width": 872,
    "height": 35.2,
    "size": 32
  },
  {
    "slide": 22,
    "text": "Paper ROOT: Total, Flux, MuonEnergyScale, StatOnly covariances \u00b7 Our validated 2D budget",
    "x": 44,
    "y": 501,
    "width": 803,
    "height": 12.2,
    "size": 10
  },
  {
    "slide": 22,
    "text": "22",
    "x": 875,
    "y": 500,
    "width": 36,
    "height": 14.64,
    "size": 12
  },
  {
    "slide": 22,
    "text": "Our energy-scale group is MINOS + MINERvA; it excludes efficiency, resolution and beam-angle terms.\nEach input uses its own bin widths. Similar source sizes do not establish identical covariance constructions.",
